{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And Jacob was incensed and he argued.</b> That is, because anger was included, argument was included as well; without this, he would not have argued." "<b>And he argued with Laban.</b> That is, relative to Laban it was evident that this was an argument, but if the matter had concerned another man it would not have been called an argument. And so you will find that they of blessed memory said (Genesis Rabbah 74), and this is their language: ״the strictness of the fathers and not the humility of the sons, etc. placations — Jacob was placating his father-in-law,״ etc., until there. And this accords with our words. Or it may further intend that he did not argue with him in a gathering of people but privately with him alone, and this is the verse's saying <b>and he argued with Laban</b> — meaning: privately with him, so as not to shame him with his reproof." "<b>What is my offense, etc.</b> Meaning: well and good — if from your days you have found in me any wrong that I offended against you, this disgrace of the theft would be through willful offense, and not only through willful offense but even through inadvertence, and this is his saying <b>what is my sin</b> that you should suspect me of theft. And Jacob revealed his thinking, that the reason for Laban's intensity was that he saw him groping through all his possessions and utensils; and since Jacob lacked knowledge of the theft of the teraphim, he would reckon that Laban was not conducting a real search but merely looking to see whether he had taken anything of his, and Laban contrived to say that his teraphim had been stolen so that he would have a pretext to search everywhere. Therefore Jacob rebuked him: from where did the side of suspicion enter into Laban that he needed to search?"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:24.070767323Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}